{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475172-vtt-for-mage","id":1475172,"title":"VTT for Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-21T19:39:23-08:00","id":1475172,"title":"VTT for Mage?","content":"Is there a VTT (virtual table top) for Mage the Ascension?<br /> <br /> The good people at OPP are opening a VTT for V5. But what would you suggest as a VTT for Mage?<br /> <br /> Direct Link: <a href=\"https://foundryvtt.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://foundryvtt.com/</a> \u201cFoundry Virtual Tabletop is a self-hosted roleplaying platform with support for hundreds of game systems with modern features and a developer-friendly API. Foundry VTT is a one-time purchase where your players connect for free using a web browser.\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T01:06:40-07:00","id":1476556,"title":"","content":"Foundry is as great as it gets, although maybe a little challenging to set up. Other than that, it's like two generations ahead of Roll20 in terms of usability, for players and STs alike. Right now I am a player in, like, 3 or 4 games hosted in a foundry setup and it just rocks - it put the fun back into online gaming, especially with the more complex games like Starfinder. But it also helps a lot with the storyteller-type games, I just lost a game of V5 \ud83d\ude25 that gained so much from the mechanics being automated and the possibilites of customizing the UI for a games mood and such.<br /> <br /> If you do NOT need rollable character sheets and game mechanics inside the VTT, maybe owlbear.rodeo might be worth a look. It's a website that lets you host your session like you're at a table - you can lay maps and/or pictures on it and move tokens around, and it even comes with a die roller (you just have to select and interpret the dice by yourself). The UI is very fantasy-centric, but the site is very easy to use and understand. It saved my sanity as a DM after being unable to jumpstart (?) in roll20 with a higher level pathfinder 1e-campaign at the beginning of the pandemic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#A52A2A\">Am I man<br /> or am I beast<br /> or am I just like you?</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1701-ags","name":"AGS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}